   "resumo_en": "Life on the Line is the second studio album by English rock band Eddie and the Hot Rods. The album was mixed by Ed Hollis and Steve Nicol, produced by Ed Hollis, and engineered by Steve Lillywhite.\nLife on the Line reached number 27 on the UK Albums Chart. The album featured three singles: \"Do Anything You Wanna Do\", which peaked at number 9 on the UK Singles Chart, \"Life on the Line\", and \"Quit This Town\", which reached number 36.\nThe song \"Do Anything You Wanna Do\" was covered by Manfred Mann's Earth Band for their Criminal Tango album (1986).",
